<http://data.silknow.org/production/3a622012-5524-3294-b68d-a139e07ea2d0>
        a                       ecrm:E12_Production ;
        ecrm:P108_has_produced  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b95ed967-7580-3785-a04e-dbdf454f5dd8> ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      "it seems like it floats over a couple of warp threads"@en , "Brocaded silk velvet with metal thread.  Pattern repeat on vertical axis with 2 minimum pattern areas.  Satin foundation structure: 4/1 satin,  warp count not taken"@en , "yellow is one strand.\nSelvedges here is interrupted"@en , "along weft 13.    Binding weft threads: silk, super-skinny white.  Brocade structure: wholly brocaded? whole  4/1 twill, count 23.  Shots between pile 2.  Metal &amp"@en , "selvedges are made of thicker warps.  At the selvedge, the brocading wefts don't extend.  The silk here looks esp short filament.  Is it possible that this is silk on silk, but the main foundation warps are made of wild silk or broken cocoon silk?"@en , "twist: silver or gilt (?) Z tightness of wrap:\nIvory brocade weft is two strand"@en , "ivory silk, no twist.  Weft: cotton, 1 strand.  Satin &amp"@en , "velvet warp order 3-1-3.  Velvet structure, red and green silk, S twist.  Pile counts, warps 10"@en ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/617> , <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/900> ;
        ecrm:P32_used_general_technique
                <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/526> ;
        ecrm:P4_has_time-span   <http://data.silknow.org/timespan/1700_1729> ;
        ecrm:P8_took_place_on_or_within
                <https://sws.geonames.org/298795/> .

